WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:05.210
- The most degrading offensive
assumption filled question

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:09.910
that I get asked way too
often, mostly on social media,

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:11.900
but perhaps maybe even in real life is,

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.220
I live a very weird life.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.520
I've spent over 10 years
studying to become a doctor.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.210
And when I finally became one,

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.730
I split my time between the hospital

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.770
and social media and media.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.790
So there's not many
doctors out there like me

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.180
and I wanna share with you what it's like

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.500
being a doctor, YouTuber,
media personality,

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.310
what does that all mean,
what challenges do I face,

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:35.410
and most importantly,

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.303
answer some of your most
frequently asked questions.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:41.840
I am a real doctor.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.970
I mean, I get that asked all the time.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:47.250
It would happen a lot more when
I was in residency training,

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.440
but now still, when I
tell people what I do,

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.060
they're like, but are you a real doctor?

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.910
I'm a true family medicine
physician, board certified.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:59.500
I keep up with my licenses,
both in New York and New Jersey,

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.050
even though I do most of my
practicing in New Jersey.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:03.170
I work half the week

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.720
in an outpatient family medicine center.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.480
I actually have done a
full day in my life video,

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:09.910
that's linked down below,

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.750
and I'm actually in
the process of shooting

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.190
another day in my life
in the coming weeks.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:16.280
I'm really excited to share that with you.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:17.720
For those of you who don't know,

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.300
being a family medicine doctor means

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:22.870
I treat patients of all ages
for all types of conditions.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:25.280
And why I love the
field of family medicine

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.730
to be in the media spotlight,

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.200
is because we have to be able to talk

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.530
on all different types of subjects.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.220
We have to digest
information from specialists,

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.530
complex information from
specialists, really quickly

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.410
and make it easily
understandable for my patients.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:44.770
I also have to predict what
questions my patients have.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.200
Oftentimes that intersect with
the questions that you have.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.710
So I think the more I practice

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.880
in being a doctor in real life,

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.460
the better I become on YouTube.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.070
But at the same time,
the more time I spend

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.940
researching different
subjects for YouTube,

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:00.960
the more value I bring to my patients.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.453
It's like one hand truly
does feed the other.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:09.920
People will see me getting
out of my car and say,

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.250
you're Dr Mike, hey Dr
Mike, I have this thing.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:13.800
Do you think I need to
go get it checked out?

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.980
Not only is that unethical that
they're doing that because,

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:20.890
you can't really make a good
diagnosis in that setting,

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:24.060
but it's also kind of like
an invasion of privacy

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.930
that I never expected to face.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:27.840
When we're in med school,
we were actually trained

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.400
to deal with something
known as cocktail medicine.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.510
And cocktail medicine is when
you're at a bar with a friend

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.770
and they say, hey you're a doctor,

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.490
let me pick your mind about something.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.530
You have to be very clear and specific

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:42.080
that you're not establishing
a doctor patient relationship.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.480
Because when you do that,

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.190
you're actually becoming
liable for the results

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.700
that they experience
in taking your advice.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.970
So you learn how to straddle this line of,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.100
explaining that you're
speaking in generalities,

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.830
you're not giving direct advice.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.440
And I've gotten better
over time in doing this,

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.250
that's why I was able to launch
my Curbside Consult Series,

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.310
where I literally run around
the streets of New York city

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:03.690
answering people's questions.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:08.000
And I've leaned into this
uncomfortable uncertain situation.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.520
And the more that I've done that,

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:10.700
the better I've become,

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:13.503
and the less stress it's
taken off of my shoulders.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.920
Now, this is very, very difficult,

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.290
but also really important

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.830
to the integrity of me as a physician.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:23.870
Unlike most influencers
or most celebrities,

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.400
when they give advice, they're
giving advice personally,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.430
but I'm giving advice not only
personally, but as an expert.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.980
So I need to understand that
the weight of my message

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.620
is higher than that of a
traditional influencer.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.800
And I need to put that extra level

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.050
of integrity on top of it.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:41.560
So you'll never see me advertise something

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:43.240
that I truly do not believe in,

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.670
or that evidence based science
doesn't stand behind as well.

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:48.720
Being financially successful is great,

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.390
but I'm never gonna do that
at the expense of my patients

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:52.513
or you, my viewer.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:59.570
My relationship with my
patients has absolutely changed

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:02.600
since I became popular, but
it's changed for the better.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.450
These are hypothetical
based on true examples.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:09.830
Patient A is a 26 year old
female that has never went

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:13.140
for a preventive health
checkup that has now come in,

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.270
and gotten her first pap smear

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.850
with a family medicine doctor,

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:18.160
because she felt comfortable

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.980
after watching a few of my videos.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:20.813
Guess what?

00:04:20.813 --> 00:04:23.370
We found an irregularity
on that pap smear.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.090
We're able to act upon that,

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:28.810
and prevent a case, a potential
future case of cancer.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:29.770
Second example.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.650
I have patients who are
looking to lose weight,

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:34.190
and they wanna do it in a healthy way,

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:35.980
they wanna see what options they have.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:38.460
Sometimes we run out of time in a visit.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.750
And they say, doctor do
you have more resources

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:41.690
for me to look at?

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:42.950
I trust your opinion.

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:45.590
Well, now I can direct them
to videos on my channel.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.780
They can watch those videos,
pick up little tidbits,

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.290
and on the next visit,

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.170
they can bring me their list of questions

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.560
so that I can answer them,

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.530
and they can make the best
decision for what works for them.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.700
And the third example, when a patient

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.120
doesn't know they're gonna see me,

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.812
I walk into the room and they freak out

00:05:02.812 --> 00:05:03.820
because they're like, my God,

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.700
I was just watching one
of your COVID-19 videos.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.340
Or I was watching one of
your Grey's Anatomy reviews.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:11.780
And now you're my actual doctor.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:15.080
And they're just so much
more dialed in on that visit.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.970
They're excited, they wanna
take control of their health.

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:21.750
I mean, that is what every
doctor wants from their patients.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.420
For them to get excited
about health literacy,

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.940
to learn about what
medications they're taking,

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.860
what preventive things
they should be doing

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:29.960
to improve their health.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:32.120
And when someone watches
that on my channel

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.860
and then sees me in the office,

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:35.640
that motivation goes through the roof.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:38.290
That's one of those things
that brings me so much joy,

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:41.490
because it oftentimes happens
in the pediatric population.

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:44.440
So when I see a 10 year
old who's struggling,

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.550
or 13 year old who's struggling in school

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.060
getting bullied perhaps,

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.040
and they feel comfortable talking to me

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.970
about their mental health struggles,

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:54.030
or what's going on at home,

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:56.763
I consider that a major, major win.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.760
When it comes to being someone
who has a lot of followers,

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:05.550
there's gonna be things
that we all share in common,

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.070
with that unique group of people.

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:08.270
Like I even talked about it

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:09.830
with Emma Chamberlain on the channel,

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.160
that interview's link down below.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.500
People recognize you,

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.130
they make assumptions about you,

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:15.680
they think they know you simply because

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.010
they saw you on the YouTube channel.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.590
When it comes to being a
popular person, I think for me,

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:22.840
one of the things that
people talk about most often,

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.060
is the loss of privacy.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:25.660
That's absolutely true.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.830
People are really involved
in your personal life,

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.810
whether it's digging
through your relationships,

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:31.370
your past relationships,

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.330
what's going on in your family life.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.120
Sometimes that gets quite weird,

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.420
especially when emails are
getting sent around to,

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.660
friends, relatives.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:45.020
I mean the amount of fake
accounts on social media

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:47.950
using my face, or my name is incredible.

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.820
Please do not fall for it.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.100
Look for the blue verified check mark.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.860
All my accounts are verified.

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:55.150
The sad part about it is,

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:57.480
they oftentimes cheat people out of money,

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:00.890
by pretending to be me,
getting them to send pictures,

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:03.070
share intimate things about their life,

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:06.060
even getting financial
benefits from doing so.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:07.790
Another thing that happens is,

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:11.190
negative comments, trolls, death threats.

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:14.170
I choose not to focus
or dwell on it so much.

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:16.510
I also think that I'm lucky.

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:19.690
There's a lot of positivity
on the channel, thanks to you.

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:21.200
I think I approach a lot of

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.680
these very difficult issues with empathy.

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:26.110
It doesn't trigger as many
people to come after me

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:27.840
in a hateful type of way.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.400
I hope to continue this
moving forward in the future,

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:33.410
where we have more fruitful discussions,

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:35.250
less hate, less trolls.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:36.083
But at the end of the day,

00:07:36.083 --> 00:07:38.300
we just have to expect for that to happen,

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.350
take it on the chin and move on.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:43.530
Because as Jonathan Haidt
said on this channel,

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:46.210
we have to become okay

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:49.420
with being treated unfairly or poorly.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:50.650
I'm probably mincing words,

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.670
but it's something similar to that.

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:54.710
And I very much agree with it.

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:58.410
And being someone who was
picked on a lot growing up,

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.780
I think I've learned
how to handle that well,

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.290
and use it in a positive way

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.540
to motivate me, to help me improve,

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.750
because ultimately that's
what we all need to do,

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:08.483
if we wanna get further in life.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.440
I studied over 10 years to get here.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.000
I did it because I love it.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.250
I'm passionate about it.

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:19.040
Nothing will ever replace
the joy that I feel

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.480
in being in a room with
a patient, helping them,

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:24.130
being one-on-one, being in that moment.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:29.130
The most degrading offensive
assumption filled question

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:33.370
that I get asked way too
often, mostly on social media,

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:34.790
why did you become a doctor

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:36.160
when you could have been a model?

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:39.070
As if those two careers
are inter-changeable.

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:40.060
When you ask that question,

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:42.690
you're almost making the
assumption in saying,

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:46.480
you can't be a doctor
who's also good-looking,

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:51.050
or you can't also be a model
and be smart at the same time.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.420
I actually just got a
few DMs the other day

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.400
from female doctors, who were saying

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:57.450
that they're struggling
with that same thing.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:00.690
The issue that people aren't
taking them seriously,

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:03.310
because they are beautiful.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:07.080
Why? Judging someone based
on their looks is useless.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:11.310
In fact, I pride myself on
proving people wrong in that.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.800
In high school I was the president

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:14.440
of the Math and Science Institute.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:18.690
It was one of the most highly
regarded types of classes

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:19.840
that we had in our school.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:21.960
Because of that, I had to
go to the principal's office

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.450
for a meeting every three months.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.080
When I'm sitting in
the principal's office,

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.260
I was dressed kind of gangster,

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:28.990
because that's how I liked to dress.

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:32.570
Baggy clothes, jeans like
falling off of my hips,

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:33.710
that was the style back then,

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:34.720
I was really into it.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.780
Principal walks into the room and says,

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:38.840
what are you here for detention?

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.290
I was like, no, I'm actually here

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:41.790
for the Math and Science Institute,

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.220
principal's bimonthly meeting.

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:46.230
I'm actually the president as well.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:50.190
The look on her face gave me goosebumps.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.690
I love that feeling.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.690
And I encourage those who
are facing the discrimination

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.350
for looking a specific way,

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:58.880
to try and use that to energize them.

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:02.100
Or, better yet something that
I've learned over time to do,

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:05.290
just prove people wrong with your results.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.070
Put blinders on, get to
where you need to be.

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:10.250
If someone is being discriminatory

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.580
because of the way you look,

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:13.120
that's a whole another
issue and you actually,

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:14.830
you should absolutely address that.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:18.240
But if someone says, you're
too beautiful to do this,

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:21.530
brush that ish off, move on

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:23.910
and crush with your
knowledge and experience.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:26.990
Check out this hilarious TikTok video

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.670
or my recent memes video
that you may have missed.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.626
And it was always, stay happy and healthy.

00:10:31.626 --> 00:10:34.126
(funky music)

